-- Tests for the Article 44-B (RAISE Act) critical safety incident encoding, with
-- expected values written by hand from the source text and a calendar. The hour
-- counting for every moment is in NOTES.md ("How the expected moments were worked
-- out"); none was copied from l4's output.
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice.
-- Every assertion here is expected to be satisfied. A failure is a finding.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `raise-domain`
IMPORT `raise-definitions`
IMPORT `raise-reporting`
IMPORT `raise-penalty`
IMPORT `raise-seat`

§ `Fixtures`

`ten to the 26` MEANS 100000000000000000000000000
`just over ten to the 26` MEANS 100000000000000000000000001
`twice ten to the 26` MEANS 200000000000000000000000000

-- UTC offsets for New York.
`EST` MEANS 0 MINUS 5
`EDT` MEANS 0 MINUS 4

-- Developer and model, fields in order: AI model, broad data set, generality, adaptable,
-- trained it, operations used so far, most operations on any foundation model, revenue.
`a frontier developer, not large` MEANS `the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 400000000
`a large frontier developer` MEANS `the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 600000000
`a developer below the threshold` MEANS `the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `ten to the 26` `ten to the 26` 600000000
`someone else's frontier model` MEANS `the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 600000000

-- Incident, fields in order: weights compromised, weights harm, conduct, materially
-- contributed, single incident, people, dollars, publicly accessible, lawful federal,
-- loss of control, loss of control harm, deception, in an evaluation, materially
-- increased risk.
`nothing happened` MEANS `the incident` FALSE FALSE `none of the three kinds of conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`stolen weights that killed someone` MEANS `the incident` TRUE TRUE `none of the three kinds of conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`stolen weights, nobody hurt` MEANS `the incident` TRUE FALSE `none of the three kinds of conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN people IS A NUMBER, dollars IS A NUMBER, public IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `the incident as I know it`
`a weapons incident with` people dollars public MEANS
    `the incident` FALSE FALSE `provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon` TRUE TRUE people dollars public FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN eval IS A BOOLEAN, risk IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `the incident as I know it`
`a deception incident with` eval risk MEANS
    `the incident` FALSE FALSE `none of the three kinds of conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE eval risk

`loss of control that killed 60 in one incident of evasion` MEANS `the incident` FALSE FALSE `evaded the control of its frontier developer or user` TRUE TRUE 60 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- Positions.
GIVEN det IS A MAYBE `a moment`, rb IS A MAYBE `a moment`
GIVETH A `my reporting position`
`in New York, with` det rb MEANS `the position` det rb FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

`13 March 2027, noon EST` MEANS `the moment` (Date 13 3 2027) 12 0 `EST`

§ `Section 1420: frontier developer, large frontier developer`

-- 10^26 exactly is not "greater than 10^26"; one more is.
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 `ten to the 26`))
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 `just over ten to the 26`
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `just over ten to the 26` 0
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `just over ten to the 26` 0))
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` 0))
#ASSERT (NOT (`the model is a frontier model` (`the developer and model` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 0)))
-- $500,000,000 exactly is not "in excess of"; one more dollar is.
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 500000000))
#ASSERT `am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `twice ten to the 26` `twice ten to the 26` 500000001
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `ten to the 26` `ten to the 26` 900000000000))

§ `Section 1420(3), (4): critical safety incident`

#ASSERT `it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights that killed someone`
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights, nobody hurt`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a developer below the threshold` `stolen weights that killed someone`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` `nothing happened`))
-- More than fifty people: 50 is not enough, 51 is.
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` (`a weapons incident with` 50 0 FALSE)))
#ASSERT `it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` (`a weapons incident with` 51 0 FALSE)
-- More than one billion dollars: 1,000,000,000 is not enough, one more is.
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` (`a weapons incident with` 0 1000000000 FALSE)))
#ASSERT `it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` (`a weapons incident with` 0 1000000001 FALSE)
-- Publicly accessible information is excluded from catastrophic risk.
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` (`a weapons incident with` 51 0 TRUE)))
-- Kind (d): not inside an evaluation designed to elicit it, and materially increased risk.
#ASSERT `it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` (`a deception incident with` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` (`a deception incident with` TRUE TRUE)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`it is a critical safety incident` `a large frontier developer` (`a deception incident with` FALSE FALSE)))
-- Kinds overlap: a loss of control in which the model evaded control and killed 60.
#ASSERT `the kinds of critical safety incident that apply` `a large frontier developer` `loss of control that killed 60 in one incident of evasion` EQUALS LIST `kind (b), harm resulting from the materialization of a catastrophic risk`, `kind (c), loss of control of a frontier model causing death or bodily injury`
#ASSERT `the kinds of critical safety incident that apply` `a developer below the threshold` `loss of control that killed 60 in one incident of evasion` EQUALS LIST

§ `Section 1422(3)(a): the 72-hour clock, minute by minute`

-- Start 2027-03-01 10:00 EST. 72 hours later is 2027-03-04 10:00 EST.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) 10 0 `EST` FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 4 3 2027) 9 59 `EST`
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) 10 0 `EST` FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 4 3 2027) 10 0 `EST`
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) 10 0 `EST` FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 4 3 2027) 10 1 `EST`))
-- Across midnight: start 2027-02-10 23:30 EST; last moment 2027-02-13 23:30 EST.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 10 2 2027) 23 30 `EST` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 13 2 2027) 23 30 `EST`
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 10 2 2027) 23 30 `EST` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 13 2 2027) 23 31 `EST`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 10 2 2027) 23 30 `EST` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 14 2 2027) 0 0 `EST`))
-- Spring forward (2:00 EST on Sunday 14 March 2027 becomes 3:00 EDT). Start
-- 2027-03-13 12:00 EST = 17:00 UTC; 72 hours later is 2027-03-16 17:00 UTC = 13:00 EDT.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 13 3 2027) 12 0 `EST` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 16 3 2027) 12 59 `EDT`
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 13 3 2027) 12 0 `EST` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 16 3 2027) 13 0 `EDT`
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 13 3 2027) 12 0 `EST` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 16 3 2027) 13 1 `EDT`))
-- Fall back (2:00 EDT on Sunday 7 November 2027 becomes 1:00 EST). Start
-- 2027-11-05 12:00 EDT = 16:00 UTC; 72 hours later is 2027-11-08 16:00 UTC = 11:00 EST.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 5 11 2027) 12 0 `EDT` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 8 11 2027) 11 0 `EST`
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 5 11 2027) 12 0 `EDT` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 8 11 2027) 11 1 `EST`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 5 11 2027) 12 0 `EDT` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 8 11 2027) 12 0 `EST`))
-- The earlier trigger governs: reasonable belief 2027-05-08 15:00 EDT, determination
-- 2027-05-10 09:00 EDT. The last moment is 2027-05-11 15:00 EDT.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 10 5 2027) 9 0 `EDT` TRUE (Date 8 5 2027) 15 0 `EDT` (Date 11 5 2027) 15 0 `EDT`
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the office within 72 hours` TRUE (Date 10 5 2027) 9 0 `EDT` TRUE (Date 8 5 2027) 15 0 `EDT` (Date 11 5 2027) 15 1 `EDT`))
-- Only the reasonable-belief trigger has happened.
#ASSERT `did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` TRUE (Date 8 5 2027) 15 0 `EDT` (Date 11 5 2027) 15 0 `EDT`
-- No clock has started.
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I report to the office within 72 hours` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST` (Date 2 1 2027) 0 0 `EST`))

§ `Section 1422(3)(a): who must report, and by when`

#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a frontier developer, not large` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`in New York, with` (JUST `13 March 2027, noon EST`) NOTHING) EQUALS `report it to the office within 72 hours` (`the moment` (Date 16 3 2027) 12 0 `EST`)
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`in New York, with` (JUST (`the moment` (Date 10 5 2027) 9 0 `EDT`)) (JUST (`the moment` (Date 8 5 2027) 15 0 `EDT`))) EQUALS `report it to the office within 72 hours` (`the moment` (Date 11 5 2027) 15 0 `EDT`)
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`in New York, with` NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS `no 72-hour clock yet, because I have neither determined that a critical safety incident occurred nor learned facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that one occurred`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights, nobody hurt` (`in New York, with` (JUST `13 March 2027, noon EST`) NOTHING) EQUALS `no duty, because the incident is not a critical safety incident`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a developer below the threshold` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`in New York, with` (JUST `13 March 2027, noon EST`) NOTHING) EQUALS `no duty, because I am not a frontier developer`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `someone else's frontier model` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`in New York, with` (JUST `13 March 2027, noon EST`) NOTHING) EQUALS `no duty, because the model is not one of my frontier models`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`the position` (JUST `13 March 2027, noon EST`) NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not covered, because the model is not developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`the position` (JUST `13 March 2027, noon EST`) NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not covered, because I am excepted under section 1426 (accredited college or university doing academic research, or Empire AI)`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`the position` (JUST `13 March 2027, noon EST`) NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `not covered, because I am excepted under section 1426 (accredited college or university doing academic research, or Empire AI)`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`the position` (JUST `13 March 2027, noon EST`) NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `deemed in compliance to the extent I meet the designated federal standard; send the office copies of the federal reports when I send them; failing that standard is a violation of the article`
-- The effective date: a clock started on 31 December 2026 is not covered; one started
-- at midnight on 1 January 2027 runs to 4 January 2027 at midnight.
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`in New York, with` (JUST (`the moment` (Date 31 12 2026) 23 59 `EST`)) NOTHING) EQUALS `not covered by this encoding, because my 72-hour clock started before the article takes effect on 1 January 2027`
#ASSERT `my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`in New York, with` (JUST (`the moment` (Date 1 1 2027) 0 0 `EST`)) NOTHING) EQUALS `report it to the office within 72 hours` (`the moment` (Date 4 1 2027) 0 0 `EST`)

§ `Section 1422(3)(b): 24 hours`

#ASSERT `did I disclose within 24 hours` (Date 1 6 2027) 8 0 `EDT` (Date 2 6 2027) 7 59 `EDT`
#ASSERT `did I disclose within 24 hours` (Date 1 6 2027) 8 0 `EDT` (Date 2 6 2027) 8 0 `EDT`
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I disclose within 24 hours` (Date 1 6 2027) 8 0 `EDT` (Date 2 6 2027) 8 1 `EDT`))
-- Across spring forward: 2027-03-13 22:00 EST = 2027-03-14 03:00 UTC; 24 hours later
-- is 2027-03-15 03:00 UTC = 2027-03-14 23:00 EDT.
#ASSERT `did I disclose within 24 hours` (Date 13 3 2027) 22 0 `EST` (Date 14 3 2027) 23 0 `EDT`
#ASSERT (NOT (`did I disclose within 24 hours` (Date 13 3 2027) 22 0 `EST` (Date 14 3 2027) 23 1 `EDT`))
#ASSERT `my duty to disclose under 1422(3)(b)` `someone else's frontier model` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`the position` NOTHING NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `disclose it within 24 hours to an appropriate authority, such as a law enforcement or public safety agency with jurisdiction, and report it to the office within 72 hours as well`
#ASSERT `my duty to disclose under 1422(3)(b)` `a large frontier developer` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`the position` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no 24-hour duty, because I have not discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury`
#ASSERT `my duty to disclose under 1422(3)(b)` `a developer below the threshold` `stolen weights that killed someone` (`the position` NOTHING NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no 24-hour duty, because I am not a frontier developer`

§ `Section 1422(1), (3)(c), (6), (9)`

#ASSERT `what must my report give` TRUE EQUALS LIST `item (a), the date of the critical safety incident`, `item (b), the reasons the incident qualifies as a critical safety incident`, `item (c), a short and plain statement describing the critical safety incident`, `item (d), whether the incident was associated with internal use of a frontier model`
#ASSERT `may I file an amended report` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`may I file an amended report` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `is my report exempt from FOIL` TRUE
#ASSERT `does complying with another regime count` FALSE EQUALS `nothing else counts: only a federal standard designated by the office, after a declaration to it, can stand in for section 1422(3), and the article gives no such effect to another state's law`

§ `Sections 1427 and 1428(5): what can happen to me`

#ASSERT `what I can be made to pay under section 1427` `a large frontier developer` `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the office within 72 hours` TRUE EQUALS `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` 1000000
#ASSERT `what I can be made to pay under section 1427` `a large frontier developer` `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the office within 72 hours` FALSE EQUALS `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` 3000000
#ASSERT `what I can be made to pay under section 1427` `a frontier developer, not large` `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the office within 72 hours` TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 1427, because I am not a large frontier developer`
#ASSERT `what I can be made to pay under section 1427` `a large frontier developer` `I failed to disclose an imminent-risk incident within 24 hours` TRUE EQUALS `a civil penalty only if section 1427 reaches a failure to disclose within 24 hours, and then only the Attorney General may recover it` 1000000
#ASSERT `what is the most the office may levy for a missing disclosure statement` 10 0 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `what is the most the office may levy for a missing disclosure statement` 30 250000 EQUALS 280000
